{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on e70a75ac (S4, the signer retires after a committed cleanup).\nI read trace fbd0e671. Yes: S4 reports that the operation cannot\nresume through this control path. No other signer finishes it.\n\nWhy. The case fails closed. The Agent's seed, bearer, grants and\nsessions are already gone, so the Agent cannot act. What remains is the\nAgent's key in the room's membership, and `revoke-key` already ends it\nwithout the first signer. A rule that lets signer J finish operation O\nof signer K is a new ownership and replay mechanism. Order fc7576f8\nparks new mechanisms, and this finding does not pay for one.\n\nThe contract:\n\n1. Every committed effect stays: the grant ends, the erased seed,\n   bearer and sessions, the tombstone of O, and the first revoke\n   envelope with its bytes. No rollback, no new signature, no deleted\n   tombstone, no signer alias.\n2. The retired or compromised signer K gets the 403 that it gets\n   today. It learns nothing more.\n3. A current authorized signer that names the same operation gets the\n   409 that it gets today, `{error: \"op\", rule: \"fingerprint\"}`, with\n   one added member `next`:\n\n   \"The cleanup of this Agent is already in effect. The key that\n   started it can no longer finish it. A member with membership.manage,\n   or the recovery key, runs revoke-key on the Agent's key.\"\n\n   Add `next` only when O is a retirement whose cleanup committed and\n   whose signer is no longer active. Every other fingerprint conflict\n   keeps its present body.\n4. The 503 text of ruling 2ef7177d stays for the ordinary case, where\n   the signer is still active.\n5. The S4 head states this limit in docs/mcp.md, where the page\n   describes retirement.\n\nTwo facts I need in your plan, not as a blocker:\n\n- What `connections` shows for this Agent after the stop.\n- Whether its row counts against any limit of the controller. If it\n  holds a place for ever, say so, and I rule on that alone.\n\nA new operation by another signer on the same Agent stays outside S4,\nas your trace says.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}